        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whether an air purifier produces ozone comes down to how it cleans. Filters make none: true HEPA and activated carbon trap pollutants without adding anything to the air. Ionizers, electrostatic, PCO and plasma units can produce some, and ozone generators produce it on purpose, at levels the EPA says can harm your lungs while doing little to clean the air.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Check the features, look for CARB certification on anything electronic, switch off ionizers you do not need, and never run an ozone generator in a room people use. For most homes, a sealed true HEPA purifier with a real carbon stage is the right answer, and it is the safest one too.
          </p>
